waila.item.panascais_caves:the_deep_mistake_scroll=Schriftrolle des tiefen Fehlers\n§9Eternal Caves Add-On\n\n§7They tunneled where no dwarf dared before.\nThe pick struck stone, but the stone bled\nblack. The mountain trembled and this was\nthe first breath "IT" took in millennia.\n§r§r
waila.item.panascais_caves:the_binding_scroll=Schriftrolle der Bindung\n§9Eternal Caves Add-On\n\n§7Five mages stood beneath the mountain's\nheart, hands trembling with grief. What\nthey forged was not art, but\nwarding-sigils drawn from pain, hammered\ninto silence.\n§r§r
waila.item.panascais_caves:the_scattering_scroll=Schriftrolle der Zerstreuung\n§9Eternal Caves Add-On\n\n§7One beast, five wards. To keep it\ndreaming, the sigils were shattered and\nburied in places no map names-where frost\ngnaws, fires weep, and nothing speaks.\n§r§r
waila.item.panascais_caves:the_glyphs_scroll=Schriftrolle der Glyphen\n§9Eternal Caves Add-On\n\n§7A stone altar listens beneath the world.\nFive marks wait-not for touch, but memory.\nThe matching must be true, or the silence\ndeepens.\n§r§r
waila.item.panascais_caves:the_awakening_scroll=Schriftrolle des Erwachens\n§9Eternal Caves Add-On\n\n§7Stein cracks. Staub breathes. The altar\ngroans beneath ancient weight. When the\nfifth mark finds its place, The Serpent\nstirs. Coils unwind, eyes open without\nlight, and the mountain forgets its\nsilence.\n§r§r
waila.item.panascais_caves:the_trial_of_flame_scroll=The Schriftrolle der Flammenprüfung\n§9Eternal Caves Add-On\n\n§7In the lakes that blaze and howl, Ember\nwaits behind walls of living fire. Only\nthe worthy walk unscorched-their path\ncools where others burn.\n§r§r
waila.item.panascais_caves:the_trial_of_water_scroll=The Schriftrolle der Wasserprüfung\n§9Eternal Caves Add-On\n\n§7Water hides where ice breathes blue and\nlight bends twice. Align the mirrors to\nreveal its shape-only perfect stillness\nsees what's real.\n§r§r
waila.item.panascais_caves:the_trial_of_wind_scroll=The Schriftrolle der Windprüfung\n§9Eternal Caves Add-On\n\n§7Wind drifts among open roots and quiet\nrivers. It does not lie still- follow the\nbreeze, and step where silence welcomes\nyou.\n§r§r
waila.item.panascais_caves:the_trial_of_earth_scroll=The Schriftrolle der Erdprüfung\n§9Eternal Caves Add-On\n\n§7Buried in the earth, beneath dust and\ngemlight. Amethyst spires and broken\ndeserts hold its shape. Only the\nheavy-hearted may lift it.\n§r§r
waila.item.panascais_caves:whispers_of_the_forgemaster_scroll=Whispers Of The Schmiedemaster Schriftrolle\n§9Eternal Caves Add-On\n\n§7It cleaves stone, splits timber, and\ncarves paths no other tool dares-\nRunenbrecher, the Schmiedemaster's last\ncreation. Not forged to fight, but to\nshape the world itself. The runes bend to\nits will. The mountain remembers its name.\n§r§r
waila.item.panascais_caves:lost_in_collapse_scroll=Im-Einsturz-Verloren-Schriftrolle\n§9Eternal Caves Add-On\n\n§7When the serpent was sealed away and the\nmountains fell silent, all records of the\nRunenbrecher vanished. Some say it lies\nburied beneath the beast itself in the\nshattered altar, waiting for a soul bold\nenough to dig deep.\n§r§r
waila.item.panascais_caves:facets_of_power_scroll=Facetten-der-Macht-Schriftrolle\n§9Eternal Caves Add-On\n\n§7Six gemstones-Saphir, Sphalerit,\nSmaragd, Rubin, Kristallopal, and Onyx-\neach forged as a fragment of dwarven\nmastery. Only when gathered can the\nancient tool be touched.\n§r§r
waila.item.panascais_caves:runes_in_stone_scroll=Runen In Stein Schriftrolle\n§9Eternal Caves Add-On\n\n§7The serpent bears five wounds hidden\nbeneath petrified coil. When it falls,\nthey open... and the gemstones call out.\n§r§r
waila.item.panascais_caves:the_forgotten_trial_scroll=Schriftrolle der vergessenen Prüfung\n§9Eternal Caves Add-On\n\n§7Im Hain, den die Zeit vergessen hat,\nschlafen Runen unter zerfallenden\nRelikten. Was die Welt vergisst, dafür\nwartet die Zeit geduldig auf die, die\ndas Verlorene suchen.\n§r§r
waila.item.panascais_caves:the_runebreaker_scroll=Schriftrolle des Runenbrechers\n§9Eternal Caves Add-On\n\n§7Setze die sechs Edelsteine in das ein,\nwas die Schlange verbirgt, und der Berg\nwird antworten. Das Relikt wird sich\nregen. Nicht mit Flamme oder Stahl -\nsondern mit lange verwehrter Macht.\n§r§r
